# Twilight Syndrome: Tansaku-hen (SLPS-00102): 16-bit little-endian codes (01 00 = あ), keys in memory byte order.
# Built from three Genkan RAM snapshots of the opening (yomikata locate + decoding against the OCR'd lines).
# Confirmed in the decoded text: hiragana あ-ん 0x01-0x2E, katakana from 0x2F (シ ン ピ ア ノ ミ カ ユ リ ト イ レ),
# が だ で ど (voiced from 0xA2), っ (small from 0x95), ョ (small katakana from 0x5F), パ (voiced katakana from 0x69),
# ー 、 「 ・ and the digits ３ ４. The rest of each block follows the same order. Kanji are 0x0100 up in scene-font order.
0100=あ
0200=い
0300=う
0400=え
0500=お
0600=か
0700=き
0800=く
0900=け
